= Instructions

Start by making London fog matcha:\
Combine @Earl Grey Matcha{1/4 teaspoon} and @Milk{1 1/2 oz} in a #Bowl{} and whisk until fully combined and frothy.

Pour the Matcha Fog into a separate vessel then pour in the other combined cocktail ingredients:
@Gin{1 1/2 oz}, @Italicus{1/2 oz}, @Lemon juice{1/4 oz}, @Simple syrup{1/2 oz}.

Rest for at least ~{15 minutes}, it should start to curdle and separate.

Pour through a #Coffee filter{}, switching vessels when it starts to run clear, 
add back in the cloudy bits back into the filter.

Measure out three onces of punch into an @Ice{} filled #Mixing glass{} and stir until chilled.

Strain into a #Rocks glass{} over some clear @Ice{}.

Garnish with a @Lemon twist{}.